  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Saint Luke the Evangelist” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, the Lord designated seventy-two others as well, and sent them in pairs before His face into every city and place where He Himself was going to come. And He said to them: “The harvest indeed is plentiful, but the laborers are few. Ask, therefore, the Lord of the harvest to send laborers into His harvest. Go: behold, I send you as lambs among wolves. Do not carry a money bag, nor a satchel, nor shoes, and salute no one along the way. Into whatever house you enter, first say: ‘Peace to this house.’ And if a son of peace is there, your peace will rest upon him; otherwise, it will come back to you. And stay in the same house, eating and drinking the things they have, for the laborer is worthy of his wage. Do not move from house to house. And into whatever city you enter and they receive you, eat what is set before you, and heal the sick who are in it, and say to them: ‘The kingdom of God has drawn near to you.’”", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w107", "w108"], "anchor": "w107", "gloss": "of his wages" }] }
  },
